% Written by the example writer (C) from the statement alone, 2 Nov 2026.
% C's note: the vocabulary has no predicate for where a registration takes
% place, so no case the statement forbids can be written. Every case is allowed.
% example:  m1 is registered once, on occasion r1. Nothing in the vocabulary says where it happened.
% expect:   allowed
member(m1).
registered(m1).
registration(r1, m1).

% example:  m1 and m2 are each registered once. Nothing in the vocabulary says where.
% expect:   allowed
member(m1).
member(m2).
registered(m1).
registered(m2).
registration(r1, m1).
registration(r2, m2).
